OFFICE OF THE MAYOR

EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 47

APRIL 1, 1980

TRANSPORTATION EMERGENCY

Whereas, All subway and bus services provided by the Metropolitan Transit Authority have ceased operations; and

Whereas, It is necessary to insure the orderly transportation of people and goods in The City of New York; and

Whereas, I find that these circumstances constitute an imminent peril to the public health and safety requiring the adoption of special rules and regulations as emergency measures;

Now, therefore, by the power vested in me as Mayor of The City of New York it is hereby ordered:

Section 1. State of Emergency. A state of emergency is hereby declared to exist with
respect to transportation within the City of New York.

§ 2. *Mahattan Traffic Restrictions.* All private passenger vehicles containing less than 2 persons are hereby prohibited from entering that portion of Manhattan situated south of 96th Street by any streets, highway bridge or tunnel.

§ 3. *Roadway Traffic Restrictions.* All private passenger vehicles containing less than 3 persons are hereby prohibited from entering and operating on the following roadways during the hours of 6 a. m. to 10 a. m. Monday through Friday:

(a) Westbound Long Island Expressway, from the Queens-Nassau County boundary to the Queens entrance to the Midtown Tunnel;

(b) Westbound Bruckner Expressway, from the Bruckner Interchange to the Tri-borough Bridge;

(c) Southbound Harlem River Drive, from Dykman Street to the FDR Drive at 125th Street;

(d) Southbound FDR Drive, from 125th Street to 73d Street;

(e) Southbound Henry Hudson Parkway, from Moshulu Parkway to 79th Street;

(f) Northbound Belt Parkway, from 4th Avenue to its merger with the Brooklyn-
Queens Expressway (60th Street);

(g) Eastbound Brooklyn-Queens Expressway, from 92d Street to Manhattan Bridge;
and

(h) Prospect Expressway northbound from Church Avenue to Gowanus Expressway.

§ 4. Enforcement. Provisions of this order shall be enforced as emergency measures under Section 8a-9.0 of the Administrative Code and shall be punishable as provided therein by a fine or imprisonment, or both. The Commissioner of Transportation may adopt such emergency rules and regulations as may be necessary to implement the provisions of this order under Section 2903(b) of the Charter; a violation of such rules and regulations shall be punishable as provided therein by a fine or imprisonment or both.

§ 5. Effective date. This order shall take effect immediately.

EDWARD I. KOCH, Mayor.

